@startuml source_control_v1.0
title F1 - Sourcing and Inventory Control

|Admin|
start
:Log in to the admin portal;
:Manage users, warehouses, regions, sales groups\n(assign Warehouse Keeper W1/W2, Sales, Retailer);

|Admin/Operator|
:Create category + SKU_A, SKU_B in Draft\n(carton unit, packaging, total shelf life);
:Enter base price + effective time\n(A = 100,000d, B = 50,000d);
if (Data valid?) then (yes)
  :Publish products;
else (no)
  :Fix in Draft;
  stop
endif
:(Optional) Create a new Draft from a published product\nif locked info must change;

|Warehouse Keeper|
:Create goods receipt\n(warehouse, SKU, quantity, production date, expiry);

|Approver|
:Review and approve the goods receipt;
if (Receipt valid?) then (yes)
  :Increase stock exactly ONCE; create/merge batch by valid data key;
else (no)
  :Reject the receipt;
  stop
endif

|Warehouse Keeper|
:Reconcile batches across W1/W2;
:Print QR labels per batch (SKU, warehouse, expiry, receipt source);
:Scan to look up a label;

partition "Lock non-sellable stock and write-off" {
  |Warehouse Keeper|
  :Report damaged lot / review expiry alert\n(quantity, reason, batch, evidence);
  |Authorized user|
  :Lock the non-issuable quantity;
  if (Locked qty overlaps Reserved?) then (yes)
    |System|
    :Block issue; flag the affected order as "Needs resolution";
  else (no)
    :Only reduce Available of the not-yet-Reserved portion;
  endif

  |Warehouse Keeper|
  :Create write-off request by batch + valid quantity;
  |Approver|
  :Approve write-off after reconciling stock and Reserved;
  :Reduce stock per document ONCE; resolve the matching locked quantity;
}

|Warehouse Keeper|
:Open the receipt - lock - write-off history of the batch;

|System|
:Hand over categories + valid stock pool (batch/QR) to F2/F3;
stop
@enduml
